<Layout title="About — Starlight Park" description="How Starlight Park combines landscape, community and thoughtful public design." prefix="../" active="about">
  <PageHero eyebrow="About Starlight Park" title="A PARK BUILT<br>AROUND <em>BELONGING.</em>" copy="More than a collection of attractions, Starlight is a connected landscape designed for curiosity, comfort and everyday use." image="friends-park.jpg" accent="green" prefix="../" />
  <section class="editorial-grid section-pad">
    <div class="large-number reveal">01</div><div class="editorial-copy reveal"><p class="eyebrow">Why it exists</p><h2>ROOM FOR NATURE.<br />ROOM FOR PEOPLE.</h2><p>Good public space should feel intuitive: easy to enter, rewarding to explore and generous enough to hold many different kinds of day. Starlight’s paths, play areas and quiet corners are conceived as one continuous experience.</p><p>The project prioritises accessible routes, resilient planting and places where visitors can meet without needing to buy anything.</p></div>
    <div class="editorial-image reveal"><img src="../images/wildflower.jpg" alt="Wildflowers and lush park planting" loading="lazy" /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="principles section-pad"><p class="eyebrow reveal">Four principles</p><div class="principle-grid"><article class="reveal"><b>01</b><h3>Open by design</h3><p>Welcoming entries, readable routes and inclusive spaces.</p></article><article class="reveal"><b>02</b><h3>Nature leads</h3><p>Ecology shapes where paths, shade and activity belong.</p></article><article class="reveal"><b>03</b><h3>Play is broad</h3><p>Movement, observation and imagination all count as play.</p></article><article class="reveal"><b>04</b><h3>Change is welcome</h3><p>The landscape is allowed to mature, shift and surprise.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="wide-image reveal"><img src="../images/valley.jpg" alt="A broad green valley beneath dramatic skies" loading="lazy" /></section>
</Layout>
